<title>POLAND: DISCOUNT HOTEL FIRM TO INVEST $350 MLN IN POLAND.</title>
<headline>DISCOUNT HOTEL FIRM TO INVEST $350 MLN IN POLAND.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish developer Echo Investment SA, the Polish subsidiary of French Sphere International SA and Dutch Copron BV set up a firm which plans to invest $350 million in building discount hotels in Poland, Echo said.</p>
<p>Echo said in a statement on Thursday that the firm planned to build 100 discount hotels in Poland in the next five years.</p>
<p>It said it had 50 percent shares of the new firm, called Hekon Hotele Ekonomiczne, but did not say how big the stakes of other shareholders were.</p>
<p>It said the hotels would later be included in the international net of Accor Group hotels.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
